  "content": {
    "title": "Rick Barnes confirms he will return as Tennessee basketball coach: 'I am'",
    "text": "March 29, 2026, 5:41 p.m. ETRick Barnes confirmed he will return to coach Tennessee basketball next season.Barnes recently received a lifetime contract from Tennessee, which automatically extends to maintain a three-year term.He has led the Volunteers to eight straight NCAA Tournament appearances.Barnes has one career Final Four appearance, which was with Texas in 2003.Rick Barnes made it clear he will be the Tennessee basketball coach next season.When Barnes was asked after the No. 6 Vols lost to No. 1 Michigan 95-62 in the Men's NCAA Tournament Elite Eight on March 29 if he’s 100% on coming back next season, he told reporters, “I am.”\"There's probably 50-some teams that'd like to be here today where we are, even after a loss,\" Barnes said. \"So I'm proud of their effort. We want more. There's no doubt we want more. We want to break through this thing, but we've got to get here first. I'm just so proud of the effort these guys gave this year.\"This was Barnes' 10th season with the Vols.In August, the 71-year-old Barnes received a lifetime contract from Tennessee.Barnes' contract sets his salary at $6 million annually. The initial term upon execution of the deal is slated to run through April 15, 2028. The contract will automatically extend every April 15 to always have three years remaining on the contract.He has taken teams to the NCAA Tournament a total of 31 times, including eight consecutive with the Vols and three straight Elite Eight appearances.His record is 36-30 in March Madness.Barnes has one Final Four appearance in his career. In 2003, Barnes and Texas lost in the Final Four, 95-84, to the eventual national champion Syracuse.In essence, the contract allows Barnes to coach at Tennessee for as long as he wants until he chooses to retire.",
